  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 13 - Else
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_else
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Else
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Sometimes a program must choose between two different actions depending
    on a condition.


    The <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font>
    statement is used to execute code only when a condition is true.

    The <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>else</color></font> statement is used when the condition
    is false.


    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color>
    value1 <color=#D4D4D4>></color> value2:</font>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>collect</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>else</color>:</font>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#F5F5AB>print</color>(<color=#CE9178>"Value 1 is Lower"</color>)</font></indent></indent>


    If
    <font="JetBrainsMono SDF">value1</font> is higher than <font="JetBrainsMono SDF">value2</font>,
    then the robot will collect the resource. Otherwise, the program will display
    a message using <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#F5F5AB>print</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>.'
  isImageBig: 0
